{{ define "home/index" }}
<main>
	<h1>gofs</h1>
	<p>
		A Go server rendering pages with <code>html/template</code>. Interactivity comes from small native web
		components that ask the server for HTML fragments and swap them into the page. No framework, no bundler,
		no runtime dependencies.
	</p>

	<section class="card">
		<h2>Examples</h2>
		<p class="muted">Each example is one page, one handler file and one or two components. Read them in this order.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><a href="/contacts">Contacts</a> — <code>&lt;live-search&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;load-more&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;edit-inline&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;row-delete&gt;</code></li>
			<li><a href="/contacts/new">New contact</a> — <code>&lt;validate-field&gt;</code>, a plain form post, and <code>&lt;app-toast&gt;</code></li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="card">
		<h2>How it fits together</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><code>internal/server/routes.go</code> — every route in one place</li>
			<li><code>internal/ui/app/pages/&lt;section&gt;/</code> — templates and their handlers, side by side</li>
			<li><code>internal/ui/app/components/&lt;tag&gt;/element.js</code> — one folder per custom element</li>
			<li><code>internal/ui/app/components/request.js</code> — the one helper components share</li>
			<li><code>internal/app/contact</code> — the backend package: domain rules and the store</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<p>
		A modal needs no component. The browser's <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> handles opening, closing, focus, the
		Escape key and the backdrop. The <code>command</code> and <code>commandfor</code> button attributes open and
		close it with no JavaScript; <code>app.js</code> provides the same behaviour for older browsers.
	</p>

	<section class="card">
		<button type="button" commandfor="example-dialog" command="show-modal">Open dialog</button>
	</section>

	<dialog id="example-dialog">
		<h2>Hello</h2>
		<p>This dialog is plain HTML. A form with <code>method="dialog"</code> closes it without a request.</p>
		<form method="dialog" class="actions">
			<button type="button" commandfor="example-dialog" command="close">Cancel</button>
			<button class="primary" value="ok">OK</button>
		</form>
	</dialog>
</main>
{{ end }}
